===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|hemlok|lang=enm}}, {{term|hemeluc|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{term|hymlic|hymlīc|lang=ang}}, {{term|hymlice|hymlīce|hemlock, bryony, convulvus|lang=ang}}, literally 'hops-like', from {{term|hymele||hop-vine|lang=ang}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{recons|humalaz|lang=gem-pro}}, {{recons|humalōn|lang=gem-pro}}, from Sarmato-Scythian {{recons|haumala|lang=xsc}}, diminutive of {{recons|hauma||ephedra; juice|lang=xsc}}, from {{etyl|iir-pro|en}} {{recons|sauma|lang=iir-pro}} from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{recons|seue-||to suck; juice|lang=ine-pro}}.

{{rel-top|cognates}}
* {{qualifier|from Proto-Germanic *humalaz, *humalōn}} {{etyl|non|-}} {{term|humall|lang=non}}, {{etyl|gml|-}} {{term|homele|lang=gml}}
* {{qualifier|from Sarmato-Scythian *haumala}} [[Ossetian]] {{term|tr=xumællæg|||hops|lang=os}}{{rfscript|Cyrillic}}
* {{qualifier|from Sarmato-Scythian *hauma}} {{etyl|ae|-}} {{term|tr=haoma|lang=ae}}{{rfscript|Avestan}}, [[Baluchi]] {{term|tr=hum|lang=bal}}{{rfscript|Arabic}}, {{etyl|fa|-}} {{term|tr=hōm}}){{rfscript|Arabic}}
* {{qualifier|from Proto-Indo-Iranian *sauma}} [[Sanskrit]] {{term|tr=soma|lang=sa}}{{rfscript|Devanagari}})
More at [[suck]].
{{rel-bottom}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any of several [[poisonous]] [[umbellifer]]ous [[plant]]s, of the genera {{taxlink|Conium|genus}} ({{taxlink|Conium maculatum|species}} and {{taxlink|Conium chaerophylloides|species}}) and ''[[Cicuta]]''.
# The [[poison]] obtained from these plants.
# Any of several [[coniferous]] [[tree]]s, of the genus ''[[Tsuga]]'', that grow in [[North America]]; the [[wood]] of such trees.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|umbellifer}} [[beaver poison]], [[devil's porridge]], [[Herb Bennet]], [[musquash root]], [[poison hemlock]], [[poison parsley]], [[spotted corobane]], [[spotted hemlock]] ''[[Conium maculatum]]''; {{taxlink|Conium chaerophylloides|species}}; {{taxlink|Conium conium maculatum|subspecies}}

